// CHOWTapeModel tape insert for the shared plugin pack. This module owns the
// tape recipe: the plugin's integer CLAP parameter ids, the 4x-oversampling
// policy, and the switches that keep the stage free of playback-head
// coloration. The recipe carries no file paths, so `tape(mix)` can build the
// whole device.
//
// Alias: `chowtape` -> CHOWTapeModel.clap in plugins.json (see README.md).
// Upstream: CHOWTapeModel 2.11.4, GPL-3.0, class org.chowdsp.CHOWTapeModel.
//
// Names below are the plugin's own controls, read from the running build with
// `muz devices inspect`.
fn tape(mix = 0.32, drive = 0.20, saturation = 0.30) = plugin("chowtape", {
    // Dry/Wet: blend of the processed tape return against the dry signal.
    p2971918811: mix,
    // Tape Drive: level into the tape transfer curve, the head-bump and
    // soft-compression region of the machine.
    p95852938: drive,
    // Tape Saturation: magnetic saturation depth, the softer counterpart to
    // the drive control.
    p113638: saturation,
    // Tone On/Off: 0 leaves the input band untouched.
    p620121635: 0,
    // Loss On/Off: 0 disables head-loss coloration.
    p1856496404: 0,
    // Wow/Flutter On/Off: 0 disables pitch wander.
    p1723790669: 0,
    // Oversampling Factor: 2 selects 4x for live playback.
    p1222066186: 2,
    // Oversampling Factor (render): 2 selects 4x for offline renders.
    p3117129981: 2
});

// The harder drive/saturation pair: same switches and oversampling, more
// record-head level. `mix` stays a caller decision.
fn driven(mix = 0.35) = tape(mix, 0.42, 0.48);
